  "name": "always_self_target",
  "description": "An always transition whose microstep leaves the snapshot unchanged (same configuration, no history recorded, no assign) is not re-selected: XState's macrostep selects eventless transitions again only after a microstep that changed the snapshot or after an internal event. A self-targeting always on an atomic state (with or without reenter) and on a compound state (which exits and re-enters its child) therefore runs once per macrostep, once more after each internal event (R raises PING), and never loops.",
